    <string name="tajweed_family_madd6_body">Madd lāzim: before a letter without a vowel or doubled, and the opening letters.</string>
    <string name="tajweed_family_madd45">Madd of 4 or 5 counts</string>
    <string name="tajweed_family_madd45_body">Before a hamza, in the word (muttaṣil) or opening the next (munfaṣil).</string>
    <string name="tajweed_family_madd246">Madd of 2, 4 or 6 counts</string>
    <string name="tajweed_family_madd246_body">Before the letter the āya stops on (ʿāriḍ, līn).</string>
    <string name="tajweed_family_madd2">Madd of 2 counts</string>
    <string name="tajweed_family_madd2_body">A long vowel written with a small letter: dagger alif, small wāw, small yāʾ.</string>
    <string name="tajweed_family_ghunnah">Ghunna, ikhfāʾ, iqlāb</string>
    <string name="tajweed_family_ghunnah_body">A nasal sound held two counts.</string>
    <string name="tajweed_family_qalqalah">Qalqala</string>
    <string name="tajweed_family_qalqalah_body">ق ط ب ج د without a vowel: the letter rebounds.</string>
    <string name="tajweed_family_tafkhim">Tafkhīm</string>
    <string name="tajweed_family_tafkhim_body">The heavy rāʾ, and the lām of the Name after a or u.</string>
    <string name="tajweed_family_silent">Not pronounced</string>
    <string name="tajweed_family_silent_body">A letter merged into the next (idghām), the joining alif, letters written and not read.</string>
    <string name="tajweed_ghunnah">Ghunna</string>
    <string name="tajweed_ghunnah_body">A doubled nūn or mīm: nasalise for two counts.</string>
    <string name="tajweed_ikhfa">Ikhfāʾ</string>
    <string name="tajweed_ikhfa_body">A nūn without a vowel, or a tanwīn, hidden before the next letter, with a ghunna of two counts.</string>
    <string name="tajweed_ikhfa_shafawi">Ikhfāʾ shafawī</string>
    <string name="tajweed_ikhfa_shafawi_body">A mīm without a vowel hidden before bāʾ, with ghunna.</string>
    <string name="tajweed_iqlab">Iqlāb</string>
    <string name="tajweed_iqlab_body">A nūn without a vowel, or a tanwīn, turned into a mīm before bāʾ, with ghunna.</string>
    <string name="tajweed_idgham_ghunnah">Idghām with ghunna</string>
    <string name="tajweed_idgham_ghunnah_body">A nūn without a vowel, or a tanwīn, merged into ي ن م و, with a ghunna of two counts.</string>
    <string name="tajweed_idgham_no_ghunnah">Idghām without ghunna</string>
    <string name="tajweed_idgham_no_ghunnah_body">A nūn without a vowel, or a tanwīn, merged into ل or ر, without ghunna.</string>
    <string name="tajweed_idgham_shafawi">Idghām shafawī</string>
    <string name="tajweed_idgham_shafawi_body">A mīm without a vowel merged into the next mīm, with ghunna.</string>
    <string name="tajweed_idgham_mutamathilayn">Idghām of two identical letters</string>
    <string name="tajweed_idgham_mutamathilayn_body">Mutamāthilayn: the first merges into the second, doubled.</string>
    <string name="tajweed_idgham_mutajanisayn">Idghām of two letters of one articulation</string>
    <string name="tajweed_idgham_mutajanisayn_body">Mutajānisayn: the first merges into the second.</string>
    <string name="tajweed_idgham_mutaqaribayn">Idghām of two near letters</string>
    <string name="tajweed_idgham_mutaqaribayn_body">Mutaqāribayn: the first merges into the second.</string>
    <string name="tajweed_qalqalah">Qalqala</string>
    <string name="tajweed_qalqalah_body">A letter without a vowel that rebounds; more clearly at a stop.</string>
    <string name="tajweed_madd_natural">Natural madd</string>
    <string name="tajweed_madd_natural_body">A long vowel of two counts.</string>
    <string name="tajweed_madd_munfasil">Separate madd (munfaṣil)</string>
    <string name="tajweed_madd_munfasil_body">A long vowel ending a word before the hamza opening the next: four or five counts.</string>
    <string name="tajweed_madd_muttasil">Joined madd (muttaṣil)</string>
    <string name="tajweed_madd_muttasil_body">A long vowel before a hamza in the same word: four or five counts.</string>
    <string name="tajweed_madd_lazim">Necessary madd (lāzim)</string>
    <string name="tajweed_madd_lazim_body">A long vowel before a letter without a vowel or doubled: six counts.</string>
    <string name="tajweed_madd_arid">Madd of the stop (ʿāriḍ)</string>
    <string name="tajweed_madd_arid_body">A long vowel before the last letter, when stopping: two, four or six counts.</string>
    <string name="tajweed_madd_lin">Madd līn</string>
    <string name="tajweed_madd_lin_body">و or ي after a fatḥa, before the last letter at a stop: two, four or six counts.</string>
    <string name="tajweed_hamzat_wasl">Joining alif</string>
    <string name="tajweed_hamzat_wasl_body">Hamzat al-waṣl: only said when a reading starts on this word.</string>
    <string name="tajweed_lam_shamsiyyah">Sun lām</string>
    <string name="tajweed_lam_shamsiyyah_body">The article\'s lām merges into the sun letter after it.</string>
    <string name="tajweed_silent">Letter not read</string>
    <string name="tajweed_silent_body">Written, not pronounced.</string>
    <string name="tajweed_tafkhim">Tafkhīm</string>
    <string name="tajweed_tafkhim_body">A letter said heavy.</string>
    <string name="recite_tajweed">Tajwīd</string>
    <string name="recite_tajweed_body">While you recite, the app measures how long you hold the long vowels, against your own natural madds: a madd of 4–5 or of 6 counts that lasts no longer than a natural one is underlined. Your stops are taken into account, and a madd held just four counts is never corrected. This check judges neither the ghunna, nor the points of articulation, nor heaviness, nor a madd held too long: timing can\'t tell those reliably letter by letter.</string>
    <string name="recite_tajweed_short45">Held %1$s s, like your natural madds (%2$s s). Before a hamza the long vowel lasts four or five counts: at least twice as long.</string>
    <string name="recite_tajweed_short6">Held %1$s s; your natural madds last %2$s s. This madd lasts six counts: three times a natural one.</string>
    <string name="recite_tajweed_how">Measured on your recitation: the time from this consonant to the next, against your ordinary long vowels.</string>
    <string name="recite_tajweed_nothing">No long vowel of 4 counts or more could be measured (it takes phrases recited without a mistake, with the new model).</string>
    <string name="recite_tajweed_some">%1$d long vowels held out of %2$d</string>
    <plurals name="recite_tajweed_all">
        <item quantity="one">%d long vowel measured, held as it should be</item>
        <item quantity="other">%d long vowels measured, all held as they should be</item>
    </plurals>
